---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AstroTerm from '../../components/AstroTerm.astro';
import { EDITOR_ORGANIZATION } from '../../lib/editorial';
import { EN } from '../../strings/en.mjs';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    ...EDITOR_ORGANIZATION,
    legalName: 'Zodiacs LLC',
    foundingDate: '2026-08-11',
  } as unknown as Record<string, unknown>,
  {
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About Zodiacs.org',
    url: 'https://zodiacs.org/about/',
    description:
      'Who runs Zodiacs.org and why: a free astrology reference where charts are computed accurately, explained plainly, and kept private on your device.',
    dateModified: '2026-09-28T00:00:00.000Z',
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="About Zodiacs.org — Accurate, Plain, Private Astrology"
  description="Who runs Zodiacs.org and why: a free astrology reference where charts are computed from real astronomy and kept private on your device."
  path="/about/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="section container container--narrow">
    <em class="kicker">About</em>
    <h1 class="method-title display">A straight answer about the sky.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Zodiacs.org is a free astrology reference built on one idea: the
        astronomy can be exact even when the interpretation is a tradition. Every
        chart here is computed from the real positions of the planets and kept on
        your own device.
      </p>

      <h2>Company</h2>
      <p>
        Zodiacs.org is the official website of <strong>Zodiacs LLC</strong>, a
        New Mexico limited liability company formed on August 11, 2026.
        Zodiacs LLC owns and operates this website and develops{' '}
        <strong>Zodiacs: Birth Chart</strong>. Company, legal, press, and support
        inquiries may be sent to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:admin@zodiacs.org">admin@zodiacs.org</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most astrology sites are either beautiful and vague or accurate and
        unreadable. The calculators that get the math right tend to look like tax
        software; the ones that feel good tend to hand-wave the numbers. We
        wanted a third option — a place where you can get your full birth chart
        in about twenty seconds, see the exact degrees behind every claim, and
        read what they mean in ordinary words.
      </p>
      <p>
        The reading comes first. Exact degrees, dated sky facts, and sources stay
        close by for anyone who wants to check them, without turning every page
        into a technical report.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy without the homework</h2>
      <p>
        When a date, degree, or birth time matters, it is calculated against the
        actual sky and checked before it appears. If you want the <AstroTerm term="ephemeris" label="ephemeris" surface="about-page" />,{' '}
        <AstroTerm term="house-system" label="house systems" surface="about-page" />, historical time-zone handling, and accuracy limits, the{' '}
        <a href="/methodology/">full methodology is public</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your data stays yours</h2>
      <p>
        The engine runs in your browser, so chart calculation sends no birth
        fields to a chart API. Charts you save live on your device; if you
        sign in to a free account, they sync to it with their birth details.
        If you explicitly attach a chart to Guide, which is offered only in
        the encrypted sync preview and not on the public site, its
        placements-only summary—not the saved name or raw birth fields—is sent
        with your question to OpenAI for that conversation; its positions still
        give your birth date and time. There are no ads and no cross-site
        tracking. The full detail is on the{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Four experiences under one roof</h2>
      <p>
        Most of the site is the astrology reference — guides, calculators,
        horoscopes, and the birthday pages. Alongside it lives{' '}
        <a href="/astrofolio/">Astrofolio</a>, a collection view of the Twelve.
        The <a href="/registry/">Zodiacs Registry</a> keeps their canonical
        records and addresses, while the <a href="/terminal/">Terminal</a>{' '}
        presents a denser record of dated public activity. These sections stay
        separate from the free astrology surfaces by design.
      </p>
      <p>
        Charts you save start on this device and sync only if you choose a
        Zodiacs.org account. Saved charts live in your profile and are never
        required to use the free tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        {EN['disclosure.aboutNotice']}{' '}
        <a href="/disclosure/">{EN['disclosure.aboutLink']}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="editorial-system">How Zodiacs.org is maintained</h2>
      <p>
        Zodiacs.org is a Zodiacs LLC publication maintained by automated systems,
        without a traditional human editorial staff. Articles use the
        Zodiacs.org organizational byline; there is no invented editor, biography,
        or set of credentials behind it. The calculators remain free because the
        core math runs on your device.
      </p>

      <details class="about-operations">
        <summary>
          <span>
            <strong>Open the publication details</strong>
            <small>Automation, checks, and public records</small>
          </span>
          <span class="about-operations__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="about-operations__body">
          <p>
            AI agents can propose writing, design, and code, but free-form model
            prose cannot publish itself. Daily editions begin with structured sky
            facts and versioned local templates. A separate astronomy audit
            recalculates the sky, while policy checks reject unsupported facts,
            unsafe certainty, and incomplete editions before publication.
          </p>
          <p>
            The current daily edition exposes its facts, generation mode, policy
            version, hashes, and verification result in a{' '}
            <a href="/data/daily-publication.json">public publication record</a>.
            The <a href="/data/editorial-constitution.json">rulebook is machine-readable</a>, the{' '}
            <a href="/methodology/#daily-publication">daily method is documented</a>, and the{' '}
            <a href="/corrections/">correction log</a> records material changes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p id="contact">
        Corrections, questions, press, or a request about your data — write to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:admin@zodiacs.org">admin@zodiacs.org</a>. If you have
        spotted an astrological or astronomical error on a page, tell us which
        page; accuracy reports are the ones we answer first.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a correction or removal request concerning a page in the People
        directory, write to <a href="mailto:people@zodiacs.org">people@zodiacs.org</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/birth-chart/"><span>Get your free birth chart</span><span class="orb">↗</span></a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/methodology/"><span>How we compute it</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .method-title { margin: 6px 0 8px; }
  .prose .lede { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--text); }
  .about-operations {
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding: 3px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--hair-1);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--void-1);
  }
  .about-operations summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 13px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .about-operations summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .about-operations summary > span:first-child { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .about-operations summary strong { color: var(--text); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .about-operations summary small { color: var(--faint); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
  .about-operations__mark::before { content: '+'; color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .about-operations[open] .about-operations__mark::before { content: '−'; }
  .about-operations__body { padding: 2px 0 4px; }
  .about-operations__body p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .about-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 36px; }
</style>
